;; M-futon-seams instance 6 — prompts as an interface.
;; Written to answer one question: does any instance of this mission exercise a
;; CONFLICT, where two incomparable patterns are enabled together and one's
;; :produces meets the other's :forbids? Instance 6 does, and the conflict is
;; not manufactured -- it is the mission's own warning, in the schema's terms.
;;
;; The mission records both halves. mfuton_prompt_override.clj's docstring:
;; "keep original prompt text in the source call sites and apply bounded
;; rewrites here". And Rob's closing note: "the switch is a transitional state,
;; not the destination ... the intended end state is the abstract path
;; absorbing the hardcoded one and the flag disappearing". Keeping the original
;; prose authoritative and generating the prose from a typed source are
;; incompatible dispositions for the same call site, and today BOTH are live.
;;
;; This instance also carries a top context, futon-theory/mission-interface-
;; signature, which instances 4, 5 and 7 do not yet have. That is deliberate:
;; it lets the two shapes be compared against clause 0's meets requirement.
;; Authored by claude-1, 2026-09-24. DRAFT pending claude-10's review.
{:schema :m-futon-seams/proto-cascade-v1
 :instance 6
 :mission-sha "0df3226e228374ddd49897be6af3f0943dd499036c84cbc5e51105d58b2c9694"

 :tokens
 {:signature-declared
  {:statement "The interface has a declared signature — what a prompt carries as typed inputs and outputs — rather than being whatever the first call site happened to write."
   :cue [1078 1146]}
  :call-sites-enumerated
  {:statement "Every call site that embeds a coupling in prompt text is listed, including the ones a grep for a literal will not find."
   :cue [12851 12920]}
  :grain-chosen
  {:statement "The unit is the prompt fragment that carries one coupling — a path, a role, a provider — not the whole packet and not the call site."
   :cue [12851 12920]}
  :original-prose-authoritative
  {:statement "The prose in the source call sites remains the authority; rewrites happen elsewhere, bounded, and only in the other mode."
   :cue [12282 12364]}
  :mode-gated
  {:statement "The change is reachable only behind an explicit mode switch, so the untouched path stays available while the new one is unproven."
   :cue [12019 12104]}
  :prose-generated
  {:statement "The typed source is canonical and the prompt prose is generated from it, so a coupling cannot be introduced by editing prose."
   :cue [13519 13599]}
  :one-authority
  {:statement "Exactly one authoritative reader for each coupling a prompt carries; any second copy is a pin read by a comparator, or a defect."
   :cue [13519 13599]}
  :replacement-discipline
  {:statement "Whatever discipline the mode flag was supplying — bounded rewrites, reviewed in one place — is installed in the same act that retires it."
   :cue [13420 13475]}
  :flag-retired
  {:statement "FUTON3C_MFUTON_MODE and the shadow module are gone; the abstract path has absorbed the hardcoded one."
   :cue [13420 13475]}}

 :initial #{}
 :want #{:one-authority :flag-retired}

